#: content/anniversaries/30/_index.md:155
msgid "…and save the world"
msgstr ""

#: content/anniversaries/30/_index.md:157
msgid ""
"**[KDE contributes to cleaning up the world](https://eco.kde.org/)** and you "
"can too. We have expanded our commitments to making a more ecologically "
"sustainable digital society. Become part of this effort joining in our **“30 "
"for 30”** program."
msgstr ""

#: content/anniversaries/30/_index.md:159
msgid "![](/fundraisers/yearend2025/konqi_katie_recycle.png)"
msgstr ""

#: content/anniversaries/30/_index.md:161
msgid ""
"KDE contributor Farid inspired us to take on the **“30 for 30”** challenge: "
"for our 30th birthday, we are asking you to create and carry out a project "
"to help the environment and make the planet a nicer place to live in. Farid "
"is planting 30 trees and we want you to come up with something similar."
msgstr ""

#: content/anniversaries/30/_index.md:163
msgid ""
"Film you and your friends and colleagues carrying out your effort and we "
"will promote your project on social media."
msgstr ""

#: content/anniversaries/30/_index.md:165
msgid "Here are some more ideas:"
msgstr ""

#: content/anniversaries/30/_index.md:169
msgid ""
"Rescue 30 computers (or more!) from ending up in a landfill by installing a "
"Free Software OS on them"
msgstr ""

#: content/anniversaries/30/_index.md:170
msgid "Upcycle 30 phones with a free mobile system"
msgstr ""

#: content/anniversaries/30/_index.md:171
msgid "Clean up 30 hectares of woodland"
msgstr ""

#: content/anniversaries/30/_index.md:172
msgid "Convert 30 people to a free operating system"
msgstr ""

#: content/anniversaries/30/_index.md:173
msgid ""
"Take 30 techbros to court so they stop polluting the air, the water, and the "
"Internet with their AI datacenters"
msgstr ""

#: content/anniversaries/30/_index.md:176
msgid "**What are you going to do? Let us know!**"
msgstr ""

#: content/anniversaries/30/_index.md:184
msgid "Plan your party🎉"
msgstr ""

#: content/anniversaries/30/_index.md:186
msgid ""
"**[Join an event happening near you](#map). If there are none, organize your "
"own!**"
msgstr ""

#: content/anniversaries/30/_index.md:188
msgid ""
"Whether it is a meetup over drinks, a nice meal with friends, an "
"installfest, or a full conference, let us know what, where, and when you are "
"celebrating KDE’s birthday."
msgstr ""

#: content/anniversaries/30/_index.md:190
msgid ""
"We’ll include your event in [our list](https://community.kde."
"org/30th_birthday) and it will show up in the map below."
msgstr ""

#: content/anniversaries/30/_index.md:194
msgid ""
"<br />**HOW TO ADD YOUR EVENT:** [Visit our wiki page](https://community.kde."
"org/30th_birthday) and add your event using the template."
msgstr ""

#: content/anniversaries/30/_index.md:202
msgid "KDE’s history"
msgstr ""

#: content/anniversaries/30/_index.md:204
msgid ""
"KDE has had a long and exciting history. Here we present a brief summary of "
"what has happened over the last few decades. If you want to see all the "
"details, visit our [timeline website](https://timeline.kde.org/), which gets "
"updated every time something important happens."
msgstr ""

#: content/anniversaries/30/_index.md:213
#, fuzzy
#| msgid "KDE Itinerary"
msgid "KDE trivia"
msgstr "KDE Itinerary"

#: content/anniversaries/30/_index.md:215
msgid "Did you know that…?"
msgstr ""

#: content/anniversaries/30/_index.md:217
msgid "…KDE has helped put robots on Mars?"
msgstr ""

#: content/anniversaries/30/_index.md:219
msgid "We did! And we have the graphical evidence to prove it:"
msgstr ""

#: content/anniversaries/30/_index.md:221
msgid ""
"![Screengrab from “Good Night Oppy” on Amazon Prime](anniversaries/30/"
"oppy_timestamped.png)"
msgstr ""

#: content/anniversaries/30/_index.md:223
msgid ""
"That is from the documentary [Good Night Oppy](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/"
"Good_Night_Oppy), about the [Opportunity Mars rover](https://en.wikipedia."
"org/wiki/Opportunity_(rover)). In the scene you can see a NASA engineer "
"troubleshooting the rover while in flight towards Mars from a KDE 3 "
"workstation."
msgstr ""

#: content/anniversaries/30/_index.md:225
msgid "You can watch _Good Night Oppy_ on Amazon Prime."
msgstr ""

#: content/anniversaries/30/_index.md:227
#: content/anniversaries/30/_index.md:240
msgid "*Submitted by Paul Brown*"
msgstr ""

#: content/anniversaries/30/_index.md:230
msgid "…KDE built the HTML engine that powers most web browsers?"
msgstr ""

#: content/anniversaries/30/_index.md:232
msgid "It’s true!"
msgstr ""

#: content/anniversaries/30/_index.md:234
msgid ""
"KDE’s web engine was written back in 1998 - 1999 and was subsequently used "
"as the basis for Apple’s Webkit and Google’s Blink engines. This means that "
"most modern browsers, including Safari, Chrome, Chromium, Microsoft Edge, "
"Opera, Vivaldi, and Brave, use KDE software at their core."
msgstr ""

#: content/anniversaries/30/_index.md:236
msgid ""
"Indeed, if you ever check out your web server’s access logs, you will see "
"“KHTML” on nearly every single line."
msgstr ""

#: content/anniversaries/30/_index.md:238
msgid "And, yes, the “K” in “KHTML” stands for “KDE”."
msgstr ""

