#: content/announcements/_index.md:0
msgid "Announcements"
msgstr "Anoncoj"

#: content/community/whatiskde/_index.md:0
msgid "About KDE"
msgstr "Pri KDE"

#: content/community/whatiskde/_index.md:6
#, fuzzy
#| msgid "What does KDE produce?"
msgid "What is KDE?"
msgstr "Kion produktas KDE"

#: content/community/whatiskde/_index.md:8
msgid ""
"KDE is an international community that has been building and distributing "
"free, open-source software for digital devices [since 1996](https://timeline."
"kde.org/). Anyone can use KDE’s software for free, or help build it."
msgstr ""

#: content/community/whatiskde/_index.md:14
msgid "What specifically has KDE built?"
msgstr ""

#: content/community/whatiskde/_index.md:16
msgid "Today KDE is best known for some of its flagship products:"
msgstr ""

#: content/community/whatiskde/_index.md:18
msgid ""
"[Plasma](https://kde.org/plasma-desktop/), a graphical desktop environment "
"for computers"
msgstr ""

#: content/community/whatiskde/_index.md:20
msgid ""
"[Krita](https://krita.org), a professional-caliber digital painting program"
msgstr ""

#: content/community/whatiskde/_index.md:22
msgid "[Kdenlive](https://kdenlive.org), a professional-caliber video editor"
msgstr ""

#: content/community/whatiskde/_index.md:23
msgid ""
"[Gcompris](https://www.gcompris.net), an educational game used in schools "
"around the world"
msgstr ""

#: content/community/whatiskde/_index.md:26
msgid ""
"These and [other pieces of KDE software](https://kde.org/products/) are used "
"by major institutions around the world, including but not limited to NASA, "
"NATO, CERN, Mercedes, the Steam Deck, the Chrome and Safari web browsers "
"(and their derivatives), various government agencies throughout Europe, "
"public schools in Brazil, Spain, and India, and the Ukrainian armed forces."
msgstr ""

#: content/community/whatiskde/_index.md:32
msgid ""
"Learn more about [who KDE software is for](https://kde.org/for/). (hint: you)"
msgstr ""

#: content/community/whatiskde/_index.md:35
msgid "KDE is about freedom"
msgstr "KDE temas pri libereco"

#: content/community/whatiskde/_index.md:37
msgid ""
"All the software that KDE produces is “free and open-source” (often called "
"“FOSS” or “FLOSS”). This means that everyone has the freedom to use, study, "
"change, and re-distribute it, free of charge. KDE software contains no ads, "
"spyware, subscription services, forced updates, secret crypto-mining or AI "
"training, or any other forms of user-hostile malware."
msgstr ""

#: content/community/whatiskde/_index.md:43
msgid ""
"See KDE’s [licensing policy](https://community.kde.org/Policies/"
"Licensing_Policy) for more information."
msgstr ""

#: content/community/whatiskde/_index.md:47
msgid "How does KDE make any money by giving everything away for free?"
msgstr ""

#: content/community/whatiskde/_index.md:49
msgid ""
"KDE is a voluntary community, not a for-profit company. The bulk of KDE "
"contributors are either volunteers, or sponsored by companies or public "
"institutions to work on KDE software."
msgstr ""

#: content/community/whatiskde/_index.md:53
msgid ""
"Nevertheless, some contributors are employed by [KDE e.V.](https://ev.kde."
"org), the German non-profit organization that legally represents KDE. To "
"fund these and other expenses (such as infrastructure, travel, and event "
"hosting), KDE e.V. receives donations from individuals and companies making "
"use of KDE software."
msgstr ""

#: content/community/whatiskde/_index.md:59
msgid ""
"KDE e.V. also manages KDE’s relationship with the <a href=\"./"
"kdefreeqtfoundation\">KDE Free Qt Foundation</a>, which governs KDE’s legal "
"arrangement with the Qt Group."
msgstr ""

#: content/community/whatiskde/_index.md:63
msgid ""
"You can make an [individual donation](https://kde.org/donate/) or become a "
"[corporate supporting member](https://ev.kde.org/supporting-members/)."
msgstr ""

#: content/community/whatiskde/_index.md:67
msgid "Is it hard to start volunteering for KDE?"
msgstr ""

#: content/community/whatiskde/_index.md:69
msgid ""
"Not at all! Every day more and more people join KDE’s ever-growing family of "
"contributors. KDE has a strong network of [resources](https://community.kde."
"org/Get_Involved/) and [mentors](https://mentorship.kde.org/), and "
"participates in student-focused programs like [Google Summer of Code]"
"(https://mentorship.kde.org/gsoc/) and [Season of KDE](https://mentorship."
"kde.org/sok/)."
msgstr ""

#: content/community/whatiskde/_index.md:78
msgid ""
"But most importantly, KDE offers the opportunity to join a software project "
"with massive worldwide impact that doesn’t make ethical compromises or get "
"bogged down by middle managers."
msgstr ""

#: content/community/whatiskde/_index.md:82
msgid ""
"By volunteering with KDE, you’ll make friends around the world and hone "
"professional skills in whatever you choose to get involved with — examples "
"include software development, graphical and UI design, project management, "
"promotion, and quality assurance."
msgstr ""

#: content/community/whatiskde/_index.md:87
msgid ""
"Of course, it also helps to have a proactive attitude and a friendly "
"personality. [Get involved today](https://community.kde.org/Get_Involved/)!"
msgstr ""

#: content/community/whatiskde/_index.md:91
msgid "What do the letters “K D E” stand for?"
msgstr ""

#: content/community/whatiskde/_index.md:93
msgid ""
"At one point, they stood for “Kool Desktop Environment”, the name of "
"versions 1-3 of KDE’s flagship desktop environment."
msgstr ""

#: content/community/whatiskde/_index.md:96
msgid ""
"The name was a riff on “CDE” (an abbreviation of “Common Desktop "
"Environment”), which at the time was a popular graphical environment for "
"UNIX workstations."
msgstr ""

#: content/community/whatiskde/_index.md:100
msgid ""
"By 2009, the people working on KDE realized that their labors had produced "
"much more than just a successful replacement for CDE; they had built an "
"entire ecosystem of free software. Thus, they decided to re-brand and gave "
"the name “KDE” to the community itself, with the graphical desktop "
"environment being renamed to “Plasma.”"
msgstr ""

#: content/community/whatiskde/_index.md:106
msgid ""
"KDE itself stands for human flourishing through free, non-exploitative, non-"
"monopolistic software, but today the letters themselves are not part of an "
"acronym and don’t have a specific meaning."
msgstr ""

#: content/contact/_index.md:0
msgid "Press Contact"
msgstr "Gazetara Kontakto"

#: content/contact/_index.md:7
msgid "Download the KDE Press Kit"
msgstr "Elŝutu la gazetaran ilaron de KDE"

#: content/contact/_index.md:9
msgid ""
"If you would like to learn more about KDE, represent us in the media, or "
"create content about KDE, our Press Kit can be a valuable resource."
msgstr ""

#: content/contact/_index.md:12
msgid ""
"The Press Kit contains a booklet with written guidelines and resources, and "
"a selection of images that can be freely used in any KDE-related content."
msgstr ""

#: content/contact/_index.md:16
msgid ""
"<a href=\"https://collaborate.kde.org/s/d8Fo5JN8xksBpTx\" class=\"button\">\n"
"Download the latest KDE Press Kit here.</a>\n"
msgstr ""

#: content/contact/_index.md:19
msgid "Get in touch with KDE's Press Room at <press@kde.org>"
msgstr "Kontaktu la Gazetaran Ĉambron de KDE ĉe <press@kde.org>"

#: content/contact/_index.md:21
msgid ""
"The people working in KDE's Press Room can help you or your media "
"organisation arrange an interview with KDE developers and contributors, "
"obtain further information about projects and people within KDE, and "
"officially contact the KDE Project. We can also provide you with statements, "
"stories, quotes, graphical material and videos for your outlet."
msgstr ""

#: content/contact/_index.md:28
msgid ""
"Unfortunately we cannot provide you with technical support, but we know who "
"can:"
msgstr ""

#: content/contact/_index.md:31
msgid ""
"If you have problems with the KDE.org website, e-mail <kde-www@kde.org>."
msgstr ""

#: content/contact/_index.md:33
msgid ""
"If you need technical support, get in touch with your operating system "
"vendor or subscribe to one of our [mailing lists](/mailinglists/) and ask "
"there. You can also check [our forums](https://discuss.kde.org/c/help/6) for "
"help."
msgstr ""

#: content/contact/_index.md:37
msgid ""
"If you are a lawyer and need contact information as required by German law, "
"go to the [Imprint](/community/whatiskde/impressum-en) ([German Impressum](/"
"community/whatiskde/impressum))."
msgstr ""

#: content/distributions.md:0
msgid "Distributions with Plasma and KDE Applications"
msgstr "Distribuoj kun Plasma kaj KDE-Aplikoj"

#: content/distributions.md:0
msgid "Choose a Linux distribution and start using KDE applications and Plasma"
msgstr "Elekti Linuksan distribuon kaj komencu uzi KDE-aplikaĵojn kaj Plasmon"

#: content/distributions.md:0
msgid ""
"This page lists some of the most popular Linux distributions with pre-"
"installed KDE software.  We recommend that you familiarize yourself with the "
"descriptions on the project sites in order to get a more complete picture."
msgstr ""
"Ĉi tiu paĝo listigas kelkajn el la plej popularaj Linuksaj distribuaĵoj kun "
"antaŭinstalita KDE-programaro. Ni rekomendas, ke vi konatiĝu kun la "
"priskriboj en la projektejoj por akiri pli kompletan bildon."

#: content/distributions.md:0
msgid "openSUSE"
msgstr "openSUSE"

#: content/distributions.md:0
msgid ""
"openSUSE comes in two versions. **Leap**, a stable distribution with regular "
"releases, comes with LTS versions of Linux, Qt and Plasma. **Tumbleweed**, a "
"rolling distribution with the latest versions of all packages\n"
"\n"
"SUSE is a KDE Patron.\n"
msgstr ""
"openSUSE venas en du versioj. **Leap**, stabila distribuo kun regulaj "
"eldonoj, venas kun LTS-versioj de Linukso, Qt kaj Plasma. **Tumbleweed**, "
"ruliĝanta distribuo kun la plej novaj versioj de ĉiuj pakaĵoj\n"
"\n"
"SUSE estas KDE-patrono.\n"

#: content/distributions.md:0
msgid "Fedora KDE"
msgstr "Fedora KDE"

#: content/distributions.md:0
msgid ""
"Fedora is a stable distribution sponsored by Red Hat. A new version of "
"Fedora is released every 6 months."
msgstr ""
"Fedora estas stabila distribuo sponsorita de Red Hat. Nova versio de Fedora "
"estas publikigita ĉiujn 6 monatojn."

#: content/distributions.md:0
msgid "Kubuntu"
msgstr "Kubuntu"

#: content/distributions.md:0
msgid ""
"Kubuntu is the Ubuntu version with KDE software by default. Developers "
"strive to provide usability for\n"
"beginners. The default installation includes many popular programs and a "
"utility for managing drivers.\n"
"\n"
"Canonical, the developer of Ubuntu and Kubuntu, is a KDE Patron.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kubuntu estas la Ubuntu-versio kun KDE-programaro defaŭlte. Programistoj "
"strebas provizi uzeblecon por\n"
"komencantoj. La defaŭlta instalo inkluzivas multajn popularajn programojn "
"kaj ilon por administri pelilojn.\n"
"\n"
"Canonical, la programisto de Ubuntu kaj Kubuntu, estas KDE-patrono.\n"

