#: content/download/_index.md:0
msgid "Getting KDE Software"
msgstr "Ekhavi KDE-Programaron"

#: content/download/_index.md:0
msgid "Learn how to install KDE Software on your device."
msgstr "Eksciu kiel instali KDE-programaron sur via aparato."

#: content/download/_index.md:7
msgid ""
"As KDE produces Free Software, you can download and install KDE programs in "
"most cases free of charge. On this page you can read about various ways to "
"get KDE software."
msgstr ""

#: content/download/_index.md:11
msgid "General Information"
msgstr "Ĝenerala Informo"

#: content/download/_index.md:13
msgid ""
"KDE software consists of a large number of individual applications, Plasma, "
"a desktop workspace to run these applications, and KDE Frameworks, a set of "
"libraries they are built upon. You can run KDE applications just fine on any "
"desktop environment. KDE applications are built to integrate well with your "
"system's components. By using also Plasma, you get even better integration "
"of your applications with the working environment while lowering system "
"resource needs."
msgstr ""

#: content/download/_index.md:22
msgid ""
"Plasma runs fine on relatively recent PCs, but it also works great on older "
"machines with more constrained resources."
msgstr ""

#: content/download/_index.md:25
msgid ""
"To install our software on Linux pick a distro and grab the packages you "
"want. See <a href=\"https://community.kde.org/"
"Get_KDE_Software_on_Your_Linux_Distro\">Get KDE Software on your Linux "
"Distro</a>."
msgstr ""

#
#: content/download/_index.md:29
msgid "KDE Plasma - Our Desktop"
msgstr "KDE Plasma - Nia Labortablo"

#: content/download/_index.md:31
msgid ""
"Installing Plasma on your system is easy if you use the major Linux "
"distributions; it's included in nearly all of them! A partial list can be "
"found here: <a href=\"https://community.kde.org/Distributions"
"\"><b>Distributions Shipping KDE Software</b></a>"
msgstr ""

#: content/download/_index.md:35
msgid ""
"There are instructions available for <strong><a href=\"https://techbase.kde."
"org/Getting_Started/Build\">building the source code</a></strong>. Building "
"from source code is not recommended for normal users as it requires "
"knowledge of software development tools."
msgstr ""

#: content/download/_index.md:41 content/products.md:0
msgid "KDE Applications"
msgstr "KDE-aplikoj"

#: content/download/_index.md:43
msgid ""
"KDE applications run fine on most Linux, BSD systems. In these cases, the "
"recommended way to install a KDE application is to use your operating "
"system's software management tool to install it. It comes included with most "
"Free operating systems."
msgstr ""

#: content/download/_index.md:49
msgid "KDE Frameworks"
msgstr "KDE Frameworks (Framoj)"

#: content/download/_index.md:51
msgid ""
"The KDE Frameworks are a set of libraries built on the Qt framework, "
"providing everything from simple utility classes to integrated solutions for "
"common requirements of desktop applications. You can download them at "
"https://download.kde.org/stable/frameworks/ or read the <a href=\"https://"
"develop.kde.org/products/frameworks/\">online documentation</a>."
msgstr ""

#: content/download/_index.md:54
msgid "Windows and macOS"
msgstr "Vindozo kaj macOS"

#: content/download/_index.md:56
msgid ""
"An installer for some KDE applications on Windows is available from <a href="
"\"https://community.kde.org/Windows\">the KDE on Windows project</a>."
msgstr ""

#: content/download/_index.md:58
msgid ""
"For Apple macOS systems, some applications have been made available by their "
"developers. A list of these can be found on the <a href=\"https://community."
"kde.org/Mac\">Community Wiki</a>."
msgstr ""

#: content/download/_index.md:60
msgid "Android"
msgstr "Android"

#: content/download/_index.md:62
msgid ""
"KDE provides some software for Android under the <a href=\"https://play."
"google.com/store/apps/dev?id=4758894585905287660\">KDE Community account on "
"the Google Play Store</a>."
msgstr ""

