"programoj."

#: content/support/_index.md:42
msgid ""
"If you’ve purchased [a product running KDE software](/hardware), first "
"contact the company that sold the product, as they may offer a warranty and "
"professional support."
msgstr ""

#: content/support/_index.md:44
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "These resources can help if you're experiencing an issue with KDE "
#| "software. If you've purchased a product running KDE software, first "
#| "contact the company that sold the product, as they may offer a warranty "
#| "and professional support. Otherwise, read on to learn how to get support "
#| "from the KDE community. Keep in mind that any such support is provided "
#| "with no warranty, by passionate volunteers. Please be kind and read "
#| "through [tips on asking questions](https://userbase.kde.org/"
#| "Asking_Questions) to learn how to ask for help in a way that maximizes "
#| "the chances of a positive outcome."
msgid ""
"Otherwise, read on to learn how to get support from the KDE community. Keep "
"in mind that any such support is provided with no warranty, by passionate "
"volunteers. Please be kind and ask for help in a way that maximizes the "
"chances of a positive outcome!"
msgstr ""
"Ĉi tiuj rimedoj povas helpi se vi spertas problemon kun KDE-programaro. Se "
"vi aĉetis produkton rulanta KDE-programaron, unue kontaktu la kompanion kiu "
"vendis la produkton, ĉar ili eble ofertas garantion kaj profesian subtenon. "
"Alie, legu plu por lerni kiel ekhavi subtenon de la KDE-komunumo. Memoru, ke "
"tia subteno estas provizita sen garantio, de pasiaj volontuloj. Bonvolu esti "
"afabla kaj tralegi [konsiletojn pri demandado](https://userbase.kde.org/"
"Asking_Questions) por lerni kiel demandi por helpo en maniero kiu "
"maksimumigas la ŝancojn de pozitiva rezulto."

